Modifications (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b) — statement of changes):

  * bilibili-redirect.bundle.js is the upstream request.bundle.js embedded
    verbatim inside a generated Egern wrapper (export default async (ctx)).
    The wrapper adds, before the upstream code runs:
      - an env_schema Toggle bridge that reads ctx.env, resolves the effective
        Host.OverseaVideo / Host.BStar / Host.PCDN / Host.MCDN / Storage /
        LogLevel values (exactly one Toggle per group selected, otherwise the
        upstream compat_arguments default), and writes them to
        globalThis.$argument in the upstream's own query-string format;
      - globalThis.$request built from ctx.request, and a
        globalThis.$persistentStore shim backed by ctx.storage;
      - an equivalent re-implementation of the four upstream host classes
        declared in url_rewrites, applied as a host/port-only substitution
        (scheme, path, query untouched) on the incoming and returned request;
      - the upstream $done(result) is captured and returned to Egern using the
        documented request-script return contract.
    The upstream bundled code itself is unmodified; no upstream line was
    edited, removed or reordered.

  * bilibili-redirect.yaml is generated from the upstream module YAML:
    name/description/compat_arguments/compat_arguments_desc/icon/homepage/
    author/open_url/mitm are taken from upstream (description and
    compat_arguments_desc get an appended note about the added Toggles),
    scriptings keep the upstream match/name and point at the generated bundle
    with the upstream {{{...}}} env preserved as a fallback, url_rewrites are
    replaced by the equivalent in-script substitution described above, and a
    new env_schema section declares one Toggle per upstream candidate value.

  * sync.py, test.mjs, README.md, NOTICE are new files by
    a13609y/egern-modules-hub (Apache License 2.0, same license as upstream).

